    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "linked-dc"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "linked dc"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " throw is 90 x 100 cm. Each stitch inserts the hook into the side loop of the previous stitch before inserting into the base, creating a horizontal link that closes the gap between stitches. The fabric is denser than regular dc with no visible holes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The linked dc works identically in all yarn weights; aran on a 5 mm hook gives a lap-throw weight. Total yardage is around 700 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Aran yarn",
              "qty": "700 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "How to work a linked dc"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Insert hook into the right-hand side loop of the previous stitch, pull up a loop. Now insert hook into the next stitch, pull up a loop (3 loops on hook). Yarn over and draw through all 3. One linked dc made."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "13 ldc x 8 rows = 10 x 10 cm in aran with a 5 mm hook. The linking tightens the stitch; gauge is closer to dc than to treble in the same yarn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
